   <!--
   =====================================================================
   WYOMING (WY) - NO STATE INCOME TAX TEST CASE
   =====================================================================

   Wyoming has NO state income tax on any type of income:
   - W-2 wages: NOT TAXED
   - Bonus income: NOT TAXED
   - Self-employment income: NOT TAXED
   - Investment income: NOT TAXED
   - All other income types: NOT TAXED

   Wyoming is one of 9 states with no personal income tax.
   The state relies on mineral severance taxes and other revenue sources.

   This test case validates energy sector worker with bonus:
   - W-2 base wages ($110,000) are NOT taxed
   - Large bonus ($25,000) is NOT taxed
   - State tax = $0 for all wage and bonus income

   Income breakdown:
   - W-2 base wages: $110,000
   - Year-end bonus: $25,000
   - Total W-2 income: $135,000

   Expected Results:
   - Federal AGI: $135,000
   - Federal Taxable: ~$105,000 (after standard deduction, MFJ)
   - Federal Tax: ~$15,000 (approximate)
   - WY State Tax: $0 (no income tax)

   Note: Bonuses are fully taxable for federal purposes but not
   subject to Wyoming state income tax (because WY has no income tax).
   =====================================================================
   -->

